#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105401 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/id #uuid "3278333b-a29e-54c5-bc94-b5525bc6f751" :question/math-academy-id "e-14617" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=8,|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta = \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}.$ Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ in terms of the vector $\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}b \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105402 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/id #uuid "58b2269d-f998-5ba5-9df8-54ea422c43aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-14618" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-3,5 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-4,0 \\rangle$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 0}{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{41}⟨5,-4,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{85}{41},-\\frac{68}{41},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105403 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "663f3f5e-56cf-5517-ba1e-d1a355767e0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14619" :question/problem "Let $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb5b189a-a239-5470-8788-4faacd32cb38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\sqrt{2},3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278140} {:answer/id #uuid "1433dd63-e106-5e2a-a9b0-9d596b00d07f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278141} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c2e29b-7068-557b-8cc7-55acec4330b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278142} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b259a5-5948-5fc3-a399-efeadb1bb56f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{9}{4},-\\frac{3}{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278143} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3df04f-5c06-5456-a867-4e13c336b9aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7c2e29b-7068-557b-8cc7-55acec4330b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278142} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d280dbb-b209-5df3-8069-73c3ea8485e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8e013a5-b3de-5807-ade4-01f7026dfed4" :question/math-academy-id "q-18377" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,-3,1⟩$ and $b=⟨\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot \\sqrt{2}+(-3)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3}⟨\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e15fe54c-65a3-5c95-bde0-75492747c438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278172} {:answer/id #uuid "7541c8ad-38ab-5c2f-ac90-24aa4e64367b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7541c8ad-38ab-5c2f-ac90-24aa4e64367b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278173} :answer-field/id #uuid "12f32dd3-ed56-5374-8c14-6d495b8663ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278171} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "619599e1-e9bd-5cbd-bc65-bf0146fc09c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "619599e1-e9bd-5cbd-bc65-bf0146fc09c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278175} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b650bda-a627-56ef-bab2-a99e8db80137" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd3150e-167c-53cf-939d-b549cc2303e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fd3150e-167c-53cf-939d-b549cc2303e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278177} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9892346-cf69-5ae3-b300-41cbbc14982e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af7b2065-ddd7-541d-b600-09c9bbc528d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-275230" :question/problem "Let $c=⟨2,-1,6⟩$ and $d=⟨4,-2,10⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 10}{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{120}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{7}{3},-\\frac{7}{6},\\frac{35}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6cefe9-ad1a-5c96-89ee-13765cab6bdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278194} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f9ca16-7042-569a-baeb-d1ce8d29aa01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d6cefe9-ad1a-5c96-89ee-13765cab6bdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278194} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e7fdc11-8a2f-532b-9337-bd8dcc7ccf8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba2dc2b6-282e-5a04-8a40-e8efff6fe0f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-275237" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot x+1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -2x+5 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ece23503-bd50-5b21-94c0-5a21dd3f5a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278219} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f3bbbd-559f-5e27-9190-64dc733578f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278220} {:answer/id #uuid "01bacc67-0858-554d-a2ad-adfed5f8dc32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278221} {:answer/id #uuid "f6da54aa-6722-520c-8d57-601765094e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278222} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7ffe4d-4b39-59ef-b4ff-61a6dce957f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{3}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01bacc67-0858-554d-a2ad-adfed5f8dc32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278221} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c9ee979-e0da-5150-9eaf-e21e2bc6decb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ba84402-0df7-51f8-9c09-70d13a0fe926" :question/math-academy-id "q-71838" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=10$, $|\\,d\\,|=2\\sqrt{3}$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={30}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d$ in terms of the vector $d.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $d:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{d}{|\\,d\\,|}=\\frac{d}{2\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & ={\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c\\cdot u \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}d\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
